        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>If we wish to sum the cubes of the first <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N]</span> integers, an easy way is to use the following formula:</p>",
            "readable_text": "If we wish to sum the cubes of the first [MATH: N] integers, an easy way is to use the following formula:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n^{3}|= 1^{3} + 2^{3} + 3^{3} + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1)^{3} + N^{3}; = (1)/(4)N^{2}(N + 1)^{2}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n^{3}|= 1^{3} + 2^{3} + 3^{3} + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1)^{3} + N^{3}; = (1)/(4)N^{2}(N + 1)^{2}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Since we also know that</p>",
            "readable_text": "Since we also know that",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n^{2}|= 1^{2} + 2^{2} + 3^{2} + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1)^{2} + N^{2}; = (1)/(6)N(N + 1)(2N + 1)]</span>\nand\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= 1 + 2 + 3 + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1) + N; = (1)/(2)N(N + 1),]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n^{2}|= 1^{2} + 2^{2} + 3^{2} + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1)^{2} + N^{2}; = (1)/(6)N(N + 1)(2N + 1)]\nand\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= 1 + 2 + 3 + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1) + N; = (1)/(2)N(N + 1),]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>we can use these formulae to evaluate any series of the form \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^N (an^3+bn^2+cn+d)}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "we can use these formulae to evaluate any series of the form\n[MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^N (an^3+bn^2+cn+d)}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Finally, it&#x27;s worth noting that</p>",
            "readable_text": "Finally, it's worth noting that",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^N n^3 = \\frac{1}{4}N^2(N+1)^2 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}N(N+1)\\right)^2 = \\left(\\sum_{n=1}^N n\\right)^2.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^N n^3 = \\frac{1}{4}N^2(N+1)^2 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}N(N+1)\\right)^2 = \\left(\\sum_{n=1}^N n\\right)^2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>In other words, the sum of the first <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N]</span> cube numbers is equal to the square of the sum of the first <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N]</span> natural numbers.</p>",
            "readable_text": "In other words, the sum of the first [MATH: N] cube numbers is equal to the square of the sum of the first [MATH: N] natural numbers.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nIf we wish to sum the cubes of the first [MATH: N] integers, an easy way is to use the following formula:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n^{3}|= 1^{3} + 2^{3} + 3^{3} + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1)^{3} + N^{3}; = (1)/(4)N^{2}(N + 1)^{2}]\n\nContent:\nSince we also know that\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n^{2}|= 1^{2} + 2^{2} + 3^{2} + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1)^{2} + N^{2}; = (1)/(6)N(N + 1)(2N + 1)]\nand\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= 1 + 2 + 3 + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1) + N; = (1)/(2)N(N + 1),]\n\nContent:\nwe can use these formulae to evaluate any series of the form\n[MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^N (an^3+bn^2+cn+d)}.]\n\nContent:\nFinally, it's worth noting that\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^N n^3 = \\frac{1}{4}N^2(N+1)^2 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}N(N+1)\\right)^2 = \\left(\\sum_{n=1}^N n\\right)^2.]\n\nContent:\nIn other words, the sum of the first [MATH: N] cube numbers is equal to the square of the sum of the first [MATH: N] natural numbers."
      },
