            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we take the factor <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> outside the summation:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^{100} 4n^3 \t= 4\\sum_{n=1}^{100} n^3]</span></p><p>Now, using the formula</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^N n^3 \t = \\frac{1}{4}N^2(N+1)^2]</span></p><p>with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N=100,]</span> we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4\u2211_(n = 1)^(100)n^{3}|= 4((1)/(4) \u22c5 100^{2}(100 + 1)^{2}); = 4((1)/(4) \u22c5 100^{2} \u22c5 101^{2}); = 4((1)/(4) \u22c5 10000 \u22c5 10201); = 4 \u22c5 25502500; = 102010000.]</span></p>",
