        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Calculate\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle\n\\sum_{n=1}^{50} (3n^3+2n).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Calculate\n[MATH: \\displaystyle\n\\sum_{n=1}^{50} (3n^3+2n).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Notice that we can write the given summation as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)(3n^{3} + 2n)|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)3n^{3} + \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)2n; = 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n^{3} + 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n]</span></p><p>Now, let&#x27;s evaluate the two series using our formulas.</p><ul><li><p>For the first series, we use the formula\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^N n^3 = \\dfrac1 4 N^2 (N+1)^2]</span>\nwith <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N=50,]</span> and we get\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n^{3}|= 3((1)/(4) \u22c5 50^{2}(50 + 1)^{2}); = 3((1)/(4) \u22c5 50^{2} \u22c5 51^{2}); = 3 \u22c5 1625625; = 4876875.]</span></p></li><li><p>For the second series, we use the formula\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^N n = \\dfrac1 2 N (N+1)]</span>\nwith <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N=50,]</span> and we get\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n|= 2((1)/(2) \u22c5 50(50 + 1)); = 2 \u22c5 1275; = 2550.]</span></p></li></ul><p>Finally, we have\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)(3n^{3} + 2n)|= 4876875 + 2550; = 4879425.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Notice that we can write the given summation as follows:\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)(3n^{3} + 2n)|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)3n^{3} + \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)2n; = 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n^{3} + 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n]\n\nNow, let's evaluate the two series using our formulas.\n\n- For the first series, we use the formula\n[MATH: \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^N n^3 = \\dfrac1 4 N^2 (N+1)^2]\nwith [MATH: N=50,] and we get\n[MATH: 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n^{3}|= 3((1)/(4) \u22c5 50^{2}(50 + 1)^{2}); = 3((1)/(4) \u22c5 50^{2} \u22c5 51^{2}); = 3 \u22c5 1625625; = 4876875.]\n- For the second series, we use the formula\n[MATH: \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^N n = \\dfrac1 2 N (N+1)]\nwith [MATH: N=50,] and we get\n[MATH: 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n|= 2((1)/(2) \u22c5 50(50 + 1)); = 2 \u22c5 1275; = 2550.]\n\nFinally, we have\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)(3n^{3} + 2n)|= 4876875 + 2550; = 4879425.]",
